    a: 'Fitbit stress tracking is a reasonable estimate of physiological arousal, not a clinical measurement. HRV, heart rate, and EDA are all validated markers of autonomic activity, but the score is a proprietary composite and can be affected by illness, caffeine, alcohol, exercise timing, and poor sensor contact. Use it to spot trends over weeks, not to diagnose anything.',
